# The Bazel targets the corpus builds in intellij-community, one label per line.
# Each is a jvm_library with Kotlin sources and no Java sources, source jars or compiler plugins. In
# their closures krusty's integration compiles every Kotlin target, mixed Kotlin and Java included,
# without source jars or compiler plugins; the rest stays on the project's JPS builder.
# They are the ones whose transitive jvm_library closures are smallest, taken in that order while the
# union of the closures holds at most about 10,000 source files, so the reference build, the krusty
# build and the warm-up fit one runner job.
